      "arabic_text": "مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ يَحْيَى عَنْ أَحْمَدَ بْنِ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عِيسَى عَنِ ابْنِ فَضَّالٍ عَنْ أَبِي الْمَغْرَاءِ عَنْ أَبِي بَصِيرٍ عَنْ أَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) قَالَ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Muhammad ibn Yahya, from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Isa, from Ibn Fazzal, from Abu al-Maghra', from Abu Baseer, from Abu Abdillah (peace be upon him) who said:"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "إِنَّ مِنْ عَلَامَاتِ شِرْكِ الشَّيْطَانِ الَّذِي لَا يُشَكُّ فِيهِ أَنْ يَكُونَ فَحَّاشاً لَا يُبَالِي مَا قَالَ وَ لَا مَا قِيلَ فِيهِ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Indeed, from the signs of the Satan's association (shirk) of which there is no doubt is that he is obscene, not caring what he says nor what is said regarding him."
      }
    }
  ],
  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "summary": "The Imam (peace be upon him) identifies a key, undeniable sign of Satanic influence or 'shirk of the Satan' as being obscene (fahhash) in speech and demeanor. This state is characterized by a lack of concern for one's own words or the words of others spoken about oneself, indicating a detachment from moral accountability.",
      "seo_question": "What is the primary sign of Satanic influence in a person's character according to Shia hadith?",
